      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُقْرُقَانُ السَّرَابِ</span></b>  <i>What is in a state of commotion,
of the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سراب</span> [or <i>mirage</i>]: (IDrd, O, K:) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السَّرَابِ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَقْرَاقُ</span></b>  means [the same, or] <i>what</i> [<i>moves
to and fro,</i> or <i>undulates,</i> or] <i>comes and goes, of
the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سراب</span>. (S.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَرَابٌ رُقْرُقَانٌ</span> [<i>Mirage</i>] <i>that
shines,</i> or <i>glistens.</i> (TA.)

